hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15982","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said, Ma'mar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas al-Jushami, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me with shabby clothes upon me, and said: Do you have wealth? I said: Yes. He said: From what wealth? I said: From all wealth; Allah the Mighty and Majestic has given me of sheep and camels. He said: Let the blessing of Allah and His honor upon you be seen. Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Shu'ba."
"15983","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said, I heard Abu al-Ahwas narrating from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) unsightly in appearance. So he said: Do you have wealth? He said: I said: Yes. He said: From what wealth? He said: I said: From all wealth, of camels and slaves and horses and sheep. So he said: When Allah gives you wealth, let it be seen upon you. Then he said: Do the camels of your people bring forth with sound ears, then you deliberately take a knife and cut their ears and say: These are buhur, and slit them or slit their skins and say: These are surum, forbidding them to yourself and your family? He said: Yes. He said: What Allah the Mighty and Majestic has given you is lawful for you, and the arm of Allah is stronger, and the knife of Allah is sharper, and perhaps he said: The arm of Allah is stronger than your arm, and the knife of Allah is sharper than your knife. He said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you see a man I stayed with who did not honor me nor entertain me, then he stayed with me; shall I recompense him for what he did or entertain him? He said: Entertain him."
"15984","Waki' narrated to us, he said, my father and Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you have wealth? He said: I said: Yes, of all wealth; Allah the Mighty and Majestic has given me of camels and horses and slaves. He said: When Allah the Mighty and Majestic gives you good, let it be seen upon you."
"15985","Ubayda ibn Humayd Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Taymi narrated to us, he said, Abu al-Za'ra narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father Malik ibn Nadla, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hands are three: the Hand of Allah the Highest, the giving hand that follows it, and the asking hand the lowest. So give the surplus, and do not be incapable concerning yourself."
"15986","Affan narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said, Abu Ishaq informed us, he said, I heard Abu al-Ahwas narrating from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) unsightly in appearance. So he said: Do you have wealth? He said: I said: Yes. He said: What is your wealth? So he said: Of all wealth, of horses and camels and slaves and sheep. He said: When Allah the Mighty and Majestic gives you wealth, let it be seen upon you. So he said: Do the camels of your people bring forth with sound ears, then you deliberately take the knife and cut them, or cut them, and say: These are buhur, and slit their skins and say: These are surum, forbidding them to yourself and your family? He said: I said: Yes. He said: All that Allah the Mighty and Majestic has given you is lawful for you, and the arm of Allah is stronger, and the knife of Allah is sharper, and perhaps he said it and perhaps he did not say it, and perhaps he said: The arm of Allah is stronger than your arm, and the knife of Allah is sharper than your knife. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man I stayed with who did not entertain me nor honor me, then he stayed with me; shall I entertain him or recompense him for what he did? He said: Rather, entertain him."
"15987","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, he said, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr informed us, from Abu al-Ahwas: that his father came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disheveled, ill in appearance. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you have wealth? He said: Of all wealth; Allah the Mighty and Majestic has given me. He said: When Allah the Mighty and Majestic bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves that it be seen upon him."
